cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its frozen 2026 market data in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Risk-Aware Trading Agents: AI trading agents for US stocks with point-in-time news backtesting"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Risk-Aware Trading Agents contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jackson-cmd/risk-aware-trading-agents"
url: "https://jackson-cmd.github.io/risk-aware-trading-agents/"
license: MIT
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
abstract: >-
  Open-source AI trading agents for US stocks that read the macro calendar, the VIX term structure and
  cross-verified news before they buy, with backtesting, paper and live trading on 10 brokers, and an MCP
  server for LLM assistants. The research kit ships a frozen, point-in-time copy of the 2026 market (daily
  prices from 2024 for 64 stocks and 25 ETFs and the VIX term structure) with SHA-256 hashes, a look-ahead
  check that re-runs every experiment with a random future, and tools to let LLM trading agents trade the
  period step by step. The headlines behind its published results (headline titles and SEC 8-K filings) are
  licensed and not distributed; their SHA-256 hashes are, and the same rules replay any news archive.
keywords:
  - trading agents
  - news backtesting
  - look-ahead bias
  - point-in-time data
  - LLM agents
  - backtesting
  - algorithmic trading
  - risk management
  - VIX
  - MCP
